{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nu={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The verification probe now runs two cases in one test: the previous slowed-timer configuration and the repository's default in-memory timers. Local construction feedback shows both cases reporting the same outcome, success with no error and the node still leading while only the non-voter is reachable, so the experiment is requeued as a successor whose comparisons cover each timer configuration separately. That removes the caveat that the earlier account rested only on artificially slowed timers.\\\",\n \\\"experiment\\\":{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"790eb5d64ed94ef5aea4736e6f66381d-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"previous_id\\\":\\\"790eb5d64ed94ef5aea4736e6f66381d-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"revision_reason\\\":\\\"Harness changed to run the isolation case twice: once with slowed heartbeat, election and lease timers and once with the repository's default in-memory timers, emitting a distinct variant for each so the comparisons can be evaluated per timer configuration.\\\",\n  \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-verifyleader\\\",\\\"s-replstate\\\",\\\"s-heartbeat\\\",\\\"s-lease\\\"],\n  \\\"scope\\\":{\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Two four-peer in-memory clusters are reduced to three voters plus one non-voter each; in each, the leader is disconnected from the two remaining voters in both directions while the non-voter stays wired, reachability is confirmed by direct AppendEntries attempts, and VerifyLeader is called. One cluster uses slowed timers and the other the repository's defaults.\\\",\n   \\\"assumptions\\\":[\n    \\\"Cluster, transports and FSM are the repository's own MakeCluster, InmemTransport and MockFSM facilities; the demotion uses the public DemoteVoter API.\\\",\n    \\\"Isolation is transport-level disconnection in both directions, confirmed by direct AppendEntries attempts recorded in the same event.\\\",\n    \\\"With default timers the leader lease may step the leader down shortly after the partition, so the verification is issued immediately after the reachability checks.\\\"\n   ]},\n  \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"For each timer configuration: start a four-peer cluster, wait for a leader and apply one command; DemoteVoter a follower so the configuration is three voters plus one non-voter; disconnect the leader from the other two voters in both directions; attempt one AppendEntries to the non-voter and one to a voter and record the errors; emit the setup event with the voters, voter quorum, reachability results, node identifiers and the variant; call VerifyLeader in a goroutine with a five-second bound and emit the result event with whether it returned, its error, whether it succeeded, the elapsed time, the leader's state and the variant.\\\",\n  \\\"requirement\\\":\\\"Leader verification must not report success unless a quorum of the voters of the configuration in force has acknowledged, under the timers the library is normally run with as well as under slowed timers.\\\",\n  \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"Raft itself: verifyLeader chooses which peers' acknowledgements count and the replication map it uses is built by the library.\\\",\n  \\\"anchors\\\":[\n   {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"s-verifyleader\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"verifyLeader\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":966,\\\"end_line\\\":966},\n   {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"s-replstate\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"startStopReplication\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":583,\\\"end_line\\\":583},\n   {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"s-heartbeat\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"heartbeat\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":388,\\\"end_line\\\":388},\n   {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"s-lease\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"checkLeaderLease\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1037,\\\"end_line\\\":1037}\n  ],\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"verify-setup-slowed\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"verify_leader_nonvoter_setup\\\",\n    \\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"variant\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"slowed-timers\\\"},\n                  {\\\"field\\\":\\\"voter_quorum\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":2}]},\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"verify-setup-default\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"verify_leader_nonvoter_setup\\\",\n    \\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"variant\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"default-timers\\\"},\n                  {\\\"field\\\":\\\"voter_quorum\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":2}]}\n  ],\n  \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"verify_leader_nonvoter_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"variant\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"verify-setup-slowed\\\",\n    \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"verify_succeeded\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n    \\\"description\\\":\\\"With slowed timers, verification fails while only a non-voter can acknowledge.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"verify_leader_nonvoter_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"variant\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"verify-setup-default\\\",\n    \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"verify_succeeded\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n    \\\"description\\\":\\\"With the library's default timers, verification fails while only a non-voter can acknowledge.\\\"}\n  ]\n }\n}\njson.dump(u,open('update.json','w'),indent=2); print('written')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
